 "notes": "km 0 = départ réel on the C-1415b ~1.5 km west of the C-17 interchange north of Granollers (neutral start 12:10 at Carrer Ramon Llull 20, Granollers, through Granollers/Canovelles/Les Franqueses); exact km-0 spot placed 7.5 km before the C-1415b/C-59 junction per the official itinéraire horaire (Generalitat PPT 'Tour horaris', 16.06.2026), so medium confidence. Spanish part follows that itinéraire point by point (C-1415b, C-59, C-1413b, N-152a, BV-5303, BV-5305, B-520, Vic, B-522, BV-5224, BV-5226, old road La Mambla, C-17/C-17z Sant Quirze–Montesquiu, C-17 tunnels, Ripoll ring, N-260, GIV-4016 via Espinosa/Fornells/Toses, local road Toses→Collada (KOM 1778 m at the junction with GI-400), GI-400 to La Molina, GIV-4082 Carretera de la Molina to Alp, C-162 via Escadarcs/Queixans, N-260 to Puigcerdà). French part has no published itinéraire; it was reconstructed from the Puigcerdà road sequence (N-260→N-152→N-154), the Département 66 press kit (communes Ur, Angoustrine-Villeneuve-des-Escaldes, Targasonne, Égat, Font-Romeu, Bolquère, La Cabanasse, Mont-Louis, La Llagonne, Matemale, Les Angles; roads RN20, RD68, RD618, RD118, RD52, RD32) and checked against the official climb data: N-154/D68 Route Neutre to the RN20 crossing, RN20 north to Ur, D618 via Villeneuve-des-Escaldes, Angoustrine, Targasonne, Égat, Font-Romeu to the Col du Calvaire (routed km 172.3–172.5 at 1836 m, climb 11.4 km/473 m reproduced on the Copernicus DEM), D618 via Pyrénées 2000 to the roundabout north of Mont-Louis, D118 over Col de la Quillane (184.0), Matemale, D52 along the north shore of Lac de Matemale, Les Angles, D32 Avenue de Mont-Louis, Route du Pla del Mir to the finish. Although Llívia is named in Catalan town lists, routing through Llívia would not fit the Calvaire climb length/km; the route only passes the exclave on the neutral road. Points whose km is not in the itinéraire (town centres, French communes, junctions) have km derived from the routed path between official points, so their km is medium confidence; unnamed '(between ...)' points are routing fill points. Routing used one-way restrictions (directed graph), so on dual carriageways the points sit on the carriageway in race direction, e.g. the northbound C-17 between Montesquiu and Ripoll with its tunnels. The itinéraire row 'Tona' (41.7) is passed on the old N-152 corridor (now C-17 / N-152a) east of the town before the race turns onto the BV-5303 to Sant Miquel de Balenyà; low confidence for that point. Between Ribes de Freser and Planès the race stays on the N-260 past Planoles; at La Molina the route crosses the resort on Avinguda de la Generalitat / Avinguda de Supermolina / Avinguda d'Alp before the GIV-4082 Carretera de la Molina descent to Alp (exact resort streets uncertain). Alp to Queixans (C-162 via Escadarcs) routes about 0.8 km shorter than the official km difference; a few other legs between official by-km rows (Santa Eugènia-Vic, Manlleu-Granollers de la Plana, Vila-seca-Borgonyà, Ribes-Planoles) also route ~0.3 km shorter, and the full routed length is ~194.6 km against 195.9 km. Straight-line distances below 60 % of the km difference occur only at hairpins (La Molina, D618 between Angoustrine and Targasonne, Route du Pla del Mir) where extra points were added. Uncertain: exact streets inside Vic, La Molina and Les Angles; km 0 spot. [geodata G: the C-17 between La Mambla and Ripoll is class motorway in Overture (Autovia Barcelona - Vic - Ripoll), which the router never uses: no path from the Farga de Bebié tunnel to the Cúbia tunnel. Its waypoints now name the class, which unlocks it within 2.5 km of them (route.py)] [geodata G: via point on the Carretera de Ribes (old N-152, Overture tertiary) east of Tona, as the notes describe: without it the router went west through Tona town (Hostalets -> Tona leg 5.98 km vs 4.0 km in the itinerary)] [geodata G: the Carretera de Ribes via point is withdrawn (it is cut off from Tona by the C-17 and caused a loop); instead the Tona point names the C-17, so the C-17 (motorway in Overture) is unlocked within 2.5 km of it: the itinerary's 4.0 km from Hostalets to Tona matches the C-17 corridor, not the 6 km through the town]",
